      'hba1c glycated haemoglobin is the percentage of the haemoglobin in your red blood cells that has glucose irreversibly stuck to it because red cells live about 120 days it reflects the average blood glucose over roughly the past 2 to 3 months weighted toward the most recent month it is not a snapshot',
